esign","pages":"1-7","publisher":"National Taiwan University of Science and Technology","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Design","volume":"18"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85215005628"],"sdg":["10. Reduced Inequalities","11. Sustainable Cities and Production","16. Peace, Justice and Strong Institutions","9. Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a6710d45-da6b-455e-93a0-fe52bc05f609"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Rethinking Design in the Public Sector : A Relational Turn","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-786183","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Quantification of a large number of compounds in the absence of authentic standards is always a challenge. More than 600 pyrrolizidine alkaloids (PAs) have been found in plants however only limited number of PAs standards are commercially available. As PAs are the most widely distributed natural plant toxins with threat to human health, risk assessment calls for quantitative analytical methods with a wide scope including PAs without available standards. In this study, a method was developed that allows simultaneous quantification of 12 PAs in the honey samples by using HPLC-HRMS with authentic standards. This method was further extended to screen for other potential PAs in the honey using multi-target screening combined with a quantitative prediction model in the cases that authentic PAs were not available. The prediction model was subsequently validated by cross-validation and additional PAs standards which were not included in the model. The maximum concentration prediction error was 50.8%.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Wang, Tingting","Frandsen, Henrik Lauritz","Roed Christiansson, Natasha","Rosendal, Sofie Elisabeth","Pedersen, Mikael","Smedsgaard, Jørn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-332635"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Smedsgaard, Jørn"],"keyword":["Honey","Pyrrolizidine alkaloids","Quantification without standards","Screening","Validation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pyrrolizidine alkaloids in honey quantification with and without standards","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/160640048/PA_in_Honey.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors acknowledge the funding from the Danish Food Authorities (Refs. Fødevareforlig 3 ) Helen Fodnæss is also acknowledged for the proof reading. The study was financially supported by the Danish Food Authorities. Appendix A"],"id":"S01-000.00-332635","identifier":[{"id":"85059296861","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-5e41655c-b1ad-4cbe-bbca-dc74427f5e70"],"keyword":["HPLC-HRMS","Honey","Pyrrolizidine alkaloids","Quantification without standards","Screening","Validation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D76E2F7D827EE80F5222B173DE3585D7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/160640048/PA_in_Honey.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Research Group for Analytical Food Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tingting","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"e52e2dd3-cc35-41dc-aa5f-0e0a33da9957","name":"Wang, Tingting","orcid":"0000-0002-9100-3447","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Lauritz","key":"frandsenpau","last":"Frandsen","locid":"7f8f5328-37cb-4aa3-a2e1-1b519b8e1c83","name":"Frandsen, Henrik Lauritz","orcid":"0000-0002-1905-8144","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Natasha","key":"roedchristianssonpau","last":"Roed Christiansson","name":"Roed Christiansson, Natasha","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"